nd Inclusive Decision for Healthy Ocean</strong></i>.&nbsp;Role: Presenter. <i>Social change, livelihoods and vulnerabilities in&nbsp;coastal&nbsp;areas in Ghana</i>.&nbsp;<strong>South African National Bioinformatics Institute, </strong>Cape Town, South Africa.</p><p><strong>23rd April, 2019:</strong>&nbsp;Validation Report Workshop, Ministry of Energy.&nbsp;<i><strong>Charcoal Value Chain in Ghana.</strong></i>&nbsp;Role: Presenter.&nbsp;<i>Charcoal value chain in Ghana – Baseline study</i>.&nbsp;Science and Technology Policy Research Institute Office, Accra, Ghana.&nbsp;</p><p>20th&nbsp;– 24th March, 2019:&nbsp;Global Challenges Research Fund-One Ocean Hub Inception Workshop.&nbsp;<i><strong>Fair and Inclusive Decision for Healthy Ocean</strong></i>.&nbsp;Role: Participant.&nbsp;University of Cape Coast, Cape Coast, Ghana.</p><p><strong>24th September, 2018:</strong>&nbsp;Ghana Sociological and Anthropological Association Conference. Social Science and Development.<strong>&nbsp;Role: </strong>Presenter.<strong>&nbsp;</strong>The changing landscape of the Kotokuraba Market of Cape Coast, Ghana: Structural design, ownership and livelihoods.&nbsp;University of Cape Coast, Cape Coast, Ghana.</p><p><strong>8th – 10th July, 2018:</strong> Ghana Food Systems Conference, Ministry of Food and Agriculture.&nbsp;<i><strong>Promoting Effective Food Systems in Ghana</strong></i>. Role: Role: Participant. University of Ghana, Accra, Ghana.</p><p><strong>3rd – 7th June, 2018:</strong> Institute of Global Law and Policy (IGLP), Conference, Harvard Law School.&nbsp;<i><strong>Political Economy Heterodoxies.</strong></i> Role: Presenter. <i>Forms and trends of Chinese capital mobility into Ghana’s agricultural sector: Beyond political economy orthodoxy</i>. Harvard Law School, Massachusetts, USA.</p><p><strong>2nd August, 2018</strong>: &nbsp;Kultur Studier-University of Cape Coast Joint Activity. <i><strong>Livelihoods in Developing Countries</strong></i>. Role: Presenter. <i>Cha