“speak up to accelerate innovation: creative work behavior spurred by servant leadership and moderated through power distance” organized by University of Professional Studies, Accra (14th - 15th December, 2023).</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><i><strong>Participant</strong></i></p><p><i><strong>&nbsp;</strong></i></p><p>1. 5th International Conference for Postgraduate Students on the theme “Transforming Communities: Postgraduate Education and Research for Resilience and Development in Africa, organized by the School of Graduate Studies, University of C ape Coast, (18th -20th March, 2025).</p><p>2. 9th Association of West African Universities Conference (AWAU) 2024 on the theme “Promoting quality tertiary education in West Africa through collaboration, regional integration and technology”, University of Cape Coast (21st - 23rd February, 2024)</p><p>3. 11th Universities, entrepreneurship and enterprise development in Africa, on the theme “Towards sustainable development in Africa: the role of universities and private sector in the African continental free trade area”, Virtual conference (8th November, 2023).</p><p>4. A workshop on “assessment” organized by School of Business, University of Cape Coast (5th June, 2023).&nbsp;</p><p>5. A three - day workshop on the theme “Grantsmanship” organized by Directorate of Research, Innovation and Consultancy, University of Cape Coast (2nd&nbsp;- 4th May, 2023).</p><p>6. Appointments and Promotions seminar on the theme “Preparations for appointments and promotion based on the 2021 criteria” organized by School of Business, University of Cape Coast (10th March, 2022).</p><p>7. 9th Universities, Entrepreneurship and Enterprise Development in Africa, on the theme “Universities, entrepreneurship and enterprise development in Africa” hosted by the University of Cape Coast in collaboration with Bonn Rhein Seig University of Applied Sciences - Germany (8th&nbsp;- 9th September, 2021).</p><p>8.A five - day continuous academic development on the theme “Structural equation modeling and qualitative research” organized by School of Business, University of Cape Coast (1st&nbsp;- 5th November, 2021).</p><p>9. 1st Joint University of Cape Coast, University of Alabama and Central University symposium on the theme “Social determinants of health” (5th&nbsp;- 6th August, 2019).</p><p>10. 4th International conference by the School of Graduate Studies of the University of Cape Coast on the theme “Changing the orientation of postgraduate education for the 21st century” (12th -14th June, 2018).</p><p>11. A two - day training programme organized by the Training and Development section of the University of Cape Coast for Research Assistants with postgraduate degree on the theme “Investigating the impact of digital tools and online resources on teaching methods” (13th&nbsp;-14th March, 2017).</p>','<p>N/A</p>','<p><i><strong>Refereed Journal Articles:</strong></i></p><ol><li>Gyensare, M. A., Soetan, G., Ogbonnaya, C., <strong>Agyapong, J. A</strong>., &amp; Roodbari, H. (2025). Sustaining employees’ thriving at work through polychronicity and work engagement: The unintended (negative) consequence of training. Journal of Occupational and Organizational Psychology, 98(1).&nbsp;<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1111/joop.70017\">https://doi.org/10.1111/joop.70017</a>. (Scopus | Q1 | Social Sciences Citation Index)</li><li>Wuaku, D. K., Koomson, S., Abraham, E. M., Markwei, U., &amp; <strong>Agyapong, J. A. M</strong>. (2025). Improving the sustainability of banks using insightful corporate governance practices: A qualitative inquiry in an emerging economy. Journal of Global Responsibility, 16(1), 120–138.&nbsp;<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1108/JGR-10-2023-0164\">https://doi.org/10.1108/JGR-10-2023-0164</a>. (Scopus | Q2 | Emerging Sources Citation Index)</li><li>Adjimah, H. P., <strong>Agyapong, J. A. M</strong>., Abiemo, M. K., &amp; Tulasi, E. E. (2025). Empowering green entrepreneurship through education: The role of self-efficacy, 